WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.178
<v NARRATOR>Jordan built the whole new-member week schedule herself, including a late-night line-up in the chapter basement.

00:00:06.178 --> 00:00:08.329
<v NARRATOR>She wasn't even there when it happened.

00:00:08.329 --> 00:00:10.370
<v NARRATOR>She was off campus at a family event.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:18.313
<v NARRATOR>So when the chapter advisor calls an exec board meeting and the fraternity and sorority life office joins in, Jordan assumes she's in the clear.

00:00:18.313 --> 00:00:19.637
<v NARRATOR>She didn't touch anyone.

00:00:19.637 --> 00:00:20.906
<v NARRATOR>She wasn't in the room.

00:00:20.906 --> 00:00:22.891
<v NARRATOR>Here's where that assumption breaks.

00:00:22.891 --> 00:00:30.503
<v NARRATOR>At least one state holds hazing activity planners responsible for their behavior even if they weren't actively involved in the act itself.

00:00:30.503 --> 00:00:32.931
<v NARRATOR>Planning the event can be enough on its own.

00:00:32.931 --> 00:00:36.571
<v NARRATOR>Jordan designed the night, set the location, set the expectations.

00:00:36.571 --> 00:00:37.454
<v NARRATOR>That's planning.

00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:41.370
<v NARRATOR>In that kind of state, criminal liability doesn't require her presence.
